Help For The Filters Menu

Filters: press f, then a key below. Available controls depend on the radio and mode.

a: Auto Notch. Press a again to switch On or Off.
b: Noise Blanker. Press b again to switch On or Off. Full stop/comma adjust level while On.
c: Contour. Press c again to switch On or Off. Full stop/comma adjust frequency while On. l selects level; w selects width; c returns to frequency. While frequency is selected, c toggles On or Off.
h: Read this help.
l: Low Cut. Full stop increases; comma decreases the lower edge.
n: Manual Notch. Press n again to switch On or Off. Full stop/comma adjust position while On; w changes width.
p: Bandwidth. Full stop increases; comma decreases. Where separate edges are required, use l and u.
q: Finish an adjustment and keep its setting; announces Done. Press q again to leave Filters; announces Back.
r: Noise Reduction. Press r again to switch On or Off. Full stop/comma adjust level while On.
u: Upper Cut. Full stop increases; comma decreases the upper edge.
v: Read filters currently On. Repeat v to review individual filter states, including Off or unknown. Another command restarts the review. Reading status changes nothing.

Adjustments stop at their limits. While a switchable filter is Off, adjustment keys leave its settings unchanged. Changes are checked by reading the radio back. Unsupported controls and unreadable settings are reported.
Radio-specific details belong in the notes for your radio under doc/supported-radios.
When bandwidth is Default, entering the control leaves it unchanged. Full stop selects the narrowest supported numeric width; comma selects the widest. Further presses step through the numeric widths. YAC confirms each change by reading the radio.
Press p for bandwidth. With separate edges, p first selects Low Cut; press p again for Upper Cut, then p to return to Low Cut. Each selection reads the current value without changing it. Comma and full stop apply each adjustment immediately, so you can hear its effect; YAC reads back and announces the result.
Noise Reduction Following Time sets how quickly the noise reduction follows changes in the received signal, where supported. It is measured in milliseconds. While this setting is selected, full stop increases the time and comma decreases it; each change is applied immediately and confirmed by readback.
In filter status reports, Not Supported means there are no supported switchable filters for the current radio and mode.

